# Frozen Round 2 protocol artifacts.
#
# The SHA-256 values recorded in docs/round_2_freeze_manifest.json are over
# these files' exact bytes, line endings included. Without pinning, Git's
# per-platform newline conversion changes those bytes on checkout and the
# freeze verification fails on a clean clone -- on Linux and macOS for the
# dataset, and on a default Windows configuration for everything else.
#
# The hashes are the frozen-protocol record and are not editable, so the
# checkout is pinned to match them instead. data/round2_ladders.jsonl is CRLF
# because it was hashed on Windows at freeze time on 2026-07-26; the rest were
# hashed as LF. The inconsistency is historical, and preserved deliberately.
#
# Verified by tests/test_freeze_manifest.py.

docs/round_2_protocol.md                    text eol=lf
scoring/round2_batch_judge_prompt.md        text eol=lf
scoring/round2_prompt_annotation_prompt.md  text eol=lf
src/analyze_round2.py                       text eol=lf
src/build_round2_dataset.py                 text eol=lf
src/generate.py                             text eol=lf
src/scoring_schema.py                       text eol=lf
requirements.txt                            text eol=lf
data/round2_ladders.jsonl                   text eol=crlf

# Regenerated by src/build_round2_dataset.py and src/audit_round2_prompts.py,
# which are frozen and so write the platform's native newline. Marking these
# as text lets Git normalize on comparison, so re-running the documented
# rebuild does not leave a spurious dirty working tree.
data/round2_pilot_prompts.jsonl             text
data/round2_prompt_audit.json               text

# Released binary artifacts: never convert.
*.npz  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
